WEBVTT

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:40.870
<i>The year is 1889.</i>

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.040
<i>Jean, Nadia and King met at the World's Fair in Paris.</i>

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.130
<i>An evil trio attacked them to get the mysterious Blue Water.</i>

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:53.130
<i>They had a narrow escape in the airplane Jean had invented.</i>

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:57.380
<i>After many adventures, they were forced to land on an island.</i>

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:02.220
<i>The island was the secret base of the mysterious Neo Atlanteans.</i>

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:05.640
<i>They met a little girl named Marie there.</i>

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:10.230
<i>But then Nadia and the others were captured by the masked Gargoyle.</i>

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:14.030
<i>He showed them an experiment of the lethal weapon, the Tower of Babel.</i>

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:18.030
<i>It was capable of annihilating an entire island.</i>

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:22.580
<i>Jean and the three villains rescued Nadia and the rest safely.</i>

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:28.750
<i>The secret base was destroyed by the mighty submarine, Nautilus.</i>

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:32.920
<i>Jean and the others decided to embark on the Nautilus.</i>

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.840
<i>Grandis fell in love with Captain Nemo.</i>

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:39.510
<i>Nemo and Nadia had been destined to meet again.</i>

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.680
<i>Nemo was also the possessor of a Blue Water.</i>

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:46.470
<i>Their new life began on the Nautilus.</i>

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:52.110
<i>Jean and the others tried to fit into a life strange to them.</i>

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:55.150
<i>After making it through attacks by Neo Atlantis,</i>

00:02:55.150 --> 00:03:00.950
<i>meeting with many people and experiencing the wonders of nature,</i>

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:05.740
<i>they finally encountered Gargoyle's space battleship.</i>

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:11.000
<i>The Nautilus was sunk by the enemy's overwhelming weaponry.</i>

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:15.040
<i>While the Nautilus was sinking into the deep sea,</i>

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:19.050
<i>Nadia learned that Nemo had brought ruin to his homeland.</i>

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.970
<i>She was badly shocked.</i>

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:28.140
<i>Nemo is destined to destroy Neo Atlantis and kill Gargoyle.</i>

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:32.520
<i>Nadia also learned that Nemo is her father.</i>

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:37.150
<i>Then the capsule carrying Nadia was cut off from the Nautilus.</i>

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:42.530
<i>The main block, with Nemo in it, vanished into the dark sea.</i>

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:45.870
<i>"Live!" is what Nemo told Nadia.</i>

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.680
What's the matter with you two?

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:08.770
Where are Sanson and Hanson?

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.930
Where did everybody go?

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.360
Why are you crying?

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.700
I'll go look for them.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:34.710
No, Marie!

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:36.540
Why not?

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.130
Nobody...

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:40.710
What?

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:44.550
Nobody is there.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.150
This isn't any fun.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.110
Let's play, King!

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:09.160
I want to play.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:13.790
I want to play with King.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.980
Where are we going?

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:40.940
Nadia...

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:53.040
Father...

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:01.590
I just wanted to stay near you.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:05.840
Yes, until your daughter, Nadia, appeared in front of us!

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.930
Why did you have to go back to being an ordinary father?

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:13.430
Why didn't you stay the man I loved?

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:15.350
Goodbye, Captain Nemo!

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.940
No! Stop it!

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:19.230
Never mind!

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:21.310
Please don't shoot!

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:28.240
What? Nemo? Doesn't Nemo mean nobody in Latin?

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:32.120
I don't like this ship.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:34.040
Here's my chance to introduce you.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:36.040
This is Nadia.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:39.120
He's a true man of the sea!

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.580
Don't you think so too, Nadia?

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.760
You seemed so absorbed in your books,

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:49.550
but I guess you find the skies more enjoyable than just pure science?

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.010
But I'm sure Captain Nemo is a nice person!

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:54.970
I think I've said too much.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:58.560
He is a jewel of the sea.
He is a man among men.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:04.650
Why? Why did you shoot him?
He was already injured!

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:08.110
He could have shot you.

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:11.070
Killer! You're inhuman!

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.780
It's no use talking to you now.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.790
You're just trying to evade me!

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:26.920
Nadia, please don't say such sad things.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:31.970
I want to play.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.600
I want to play.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:38.890
I want to play with King.

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:47.320
Nadia, look over here!

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:51.280
This is great! These are called encyclopedias.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.160
Everything about the world is written in these.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:58.870
Look! Philosophy, religion, literature, medicine and history.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:01.370
There are volumes about physics, chemistry, Earth and space.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:04.420
A Who's Who and the world map are in independent volumes.

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:07.000
Everything you'd want to know is in these books!

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.960
Then tell me what will happen to us next!

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:13.930
We're trapped in a place like this!

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:17.100
We don't know where to go! We might sink into the deep sea!

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:20.930
Moreover, Gargoyle could be waiting for us on the surface.

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:24.650
You said everything is written in those books! Then tell me!

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:26.940
Don't worry.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:30.610
We'll be on the surface soon with the buoyant force.

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:33.450
There are emergency rations in this room too.

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:38.780
This room is made of space titanium.
We don't have to worry about anything.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:44.040
We've been bombed so much! Water can gush in at any time!

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:48.710
See? I told you!

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.590
Oh, no!

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:02.850
It seems this room received a lot of damage.

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:06.440
Any shock could cause a flood.

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:10.480
We'd better keep quiet. We shouldn't move much.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.360
That's true.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:13.030
Marie understands!

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:26.500
Still not yet?

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:27.790
Not yet.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:42.770
I want to play. I want to play.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:04.540
I think I'm catching a cold.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:18.880
That's why I can't believe in science!

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.550
Darn you, Jean!

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.810
You've got to do something!

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:25.310
Right! I'm a man after all!

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:39.410
Jean, you're amazing! I never would have expected that from you.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:42.280
See, I can do something right.

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:49.540
No!

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:03.720
I'm sorry I sneezed. I... I just couldn't help it.

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:11.900
We're sure to drown now.

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:14.110
All right! Let's open this hatch!

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:19.650
But water will gush in if we open it.

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:22.410
Even Marie and King know that.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.070
Oh, no, no, no.

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:28.750
Listen. If water comes in, the air will go out at the same time.

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:30.580
And?

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:31.580
This!

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:35.250
Air is lighter than water,

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:37.170
so it will go up to the surface.

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:42.380
We gather the air under this umbrella,

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:45.640
and then put our heads there.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:51.520
The air under the umbrella will be kept there. We can go up with the air.

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:55.150
Well? Isn't that a good idea?

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:58.230
Amazing, Jean! It's a very good idea!

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:01.950
Miss Electra told me we must try to find a way out of every difficulty.

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:04.780
I see.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:13.580
Ready?

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:17.840
One! Two!

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:19.340
Three!

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.000
Are we safe?

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:57.880
Looks like it.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:00.420
We didn't need to worry...

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.360
Say, Jean...

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.280
Where are we?

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.290
Could it be Africa?

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:45.130
No, that type of palm tree doesn't grow in Africa.

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.090
Oh...

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:48.590
That's a pity.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:04.860
Don't destroy it, King.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:07.320
It's nice to see children.

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:11.160
What are you talking about?
You're still a kid.

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:16.500
Geez! Why are you jumping on me?
You're a kid too.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:22.090
I didn't have time growing up to be a kid.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.050
I'm sorry.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:29.640
I'm sorry too. You grew up the same way, didn't you?

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:32.390
Let's go, Nadia!

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:35.520
Maybe we can find a village.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:36.230
Yes!

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:37.270
Nadia!

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:40.230
Look, look!

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:42.900
I found this.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:46.570
I found a lot of them!

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:50.030
Canned food for Gargoyle's men!

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:51.570
Where did you find it, Marie?

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:52.780
There!

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:54.410
Nadia...

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:56.620
Are there more of Gargoyle's bases?

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:57.960
Let's find out.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:00.420
Yes...

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:07.510
What's this?

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:10.380
I don't know. Some wreckage, I guess.

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:15.060
What's that?

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:17.060
A Garfish!

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:23.310
Gargoyle could be there.

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:25.770
Yes. It'd be awful if he were near here.

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:27.940
What? Nobody's here.

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:36.830
Did they have a fight with the Nautilus?

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:42.540
I suppose. The Nautilus is the only ship that could beat a Garfish.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.300
Marie, don't run off. It's too dangerous!

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:49.470
It's okay! Come on, King!

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:50.510
Marie!

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:52.050
She'll be okay.

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:58.600
The rust tells me that one month has passed.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:02.850
If someone was alive, they wouldn't leave these cans of food here.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.360
They must have gone to some town.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:09.690
You mean there's a town around here?

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:43.100
What?

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:44.310
What's wrong, Jean?

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:47.190
This is the same place we started.

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:49.230
Why do you say that?

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:51.320
Look!

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:53.110
Oh, no.

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:53.700
See?

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:55.280
Nadia!

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:57.240
Yeah!

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:00.240
I found another one!

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:03.910
That must mean...

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:08.380
This... is an island!

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:14.220
Any sign of human beings?

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:18.010
No sign of anyone?

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.650
That must mean...

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:29.900
This is a desert island!

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:51.840
Why am I so unlucky?

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:58.300
I just want to go to Africa, not some desert island!

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:01.720
Uncle must be worried.

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:05.180
He might be thinking I'm already dead.

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:10.150
Grandis and the others flew away too.

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:13.690
Did they escape on the Gratan?

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:18.240
What was the propeller they used that time? Did Hanson invent it?

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:23.580
They were evil people after all. They got what they deserved.

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:26.460
I envy Hanson.

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.880
I wish I could create something useful.

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:34.630
There are more important things than inventions.

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:44.770
I'm hungry.

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:50.560
We should find something to eat soon, before it gets dark.

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:55.690
It's so far...

00:18:59.570 --> 00:18:59.910
We can't even eat...

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:03.030
Nadia! Jean!

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:04.280
Oh, yeah! Let Marie and King...

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:06.750
Nadia! Jean!

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:09.330
A ship!

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:12.750
There, there!

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:14.170
Where?

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:15.710
Over there!

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:28.390
Ahoy!

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:33.560
It's no use, Jean. They can't hear us!

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:36.070
Don't give up so easily!

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:37.530
Just watch!

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:47.240
AHOY!

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:10.640
It's no use after all.

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:22.150
I'm so hungry.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:23.530
Yeah...

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:29.200
Here!

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:33.080
Oh, this is an emergency ration from the Nautilus!

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:35.460
Where did you get this?

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:37.590
I brought it.

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:39.880
How?

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:42.050
On foot.

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:43.760
On foot?

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:49.600
See? We can walk to it.

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:52.770
The tide has ebbed.

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:54.440
So it seems.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:02.070
Oh, no!

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:03.200
What's wrong?

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:05.780
We don't have a can opener!

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:10.990
I don't care. I can't eat them anyway.

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:14.330
But we'll starve to death!

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:17.130
Jean, King can do it.

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:19.460
How?

00:21:43.490 --> 00:21:45.110
That'll kill you, King!

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:54.450
King!

00:21:54.450 --> 00:21:55.960
Don't eat our food!

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:02.380
Let's eat!

00:22:02.380 --> 00:22:05.090
You had enough, didn't you, King?

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:07.380
We'll leave this job to you, King!

00:22:13.600 --> 00:22:15.890
You can eat this, Nadia.

00:22:15.890 --> 00:22:17.770
What's this?

00:22:18.140 --> 00:22:20.730
Fried chopped potatoes.

00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:27.450
Delicious!

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:28.740
Really?

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:29.360
Yeah!

00:22:29.990 --> 00:22:33.580
But it's seasoned just like meat.

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:38.290
Who cares? It's just seasoning, right? So it's all right to eat.

00:22:38.290 --> 00:22:40.710
Geez! It's just a matter of likes and dislikes then.

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:44.840
Oh, yes! Likes and dislikes!
Likes and dislikes!

00:22:44.840 --> 00:22:46.300
Never mind!

00:23:04.650 --> 00:23:05.690
Don't step on it.

00:23:06.610 --> 00:23:08.400
What are you doing?

00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:13.160
I'm trying to find the location of this island by the position of the stars.

00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:16.490
Nadia!

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:25.090
It's okay. You don't need to do that.

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:26.920
Nadia...

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:30.840
We're the only ones on this island.

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:34.390
There's no one evil, or anyone I hate here.

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:39.390
If Marie and King are with me,

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:41.560
I can spend the rest of my life on this island.

00:23:42.650 --> 00:23:43.440
Nadia...

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:49.650
What about me?
